---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Flip Phillips" description="Bio, career trajectory, appointments, and research background of Flip Phillips.">
  <div class="py-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold">
        Biographical Overview
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 mt-1">
        About Flip Phillips
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300 font-serif italic mt-2">
        Professor of Motion Picture Science &bull; School of Film & Animation & Center for Imaging Science &bull; RIT
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert prose-lg font-sans
      prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:font-bold
      prose-a:text-blue-600 dark:prose-a:text-blue-400 prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline">
      
      <div class="my-6">
        <img
          src="/images/uploads/2017/03/L1000017.jpg"
          alt="Flip Phillips portrait by Roland Fleming"
          class="rounded-2xl shadow-lg w-full max-h-[500px] object-cover"
        />
        <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 font-mono mt-2 text-center">Portrait by Roland Fleming</p>
      </div>

      <p class="lead text-xl text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 leading-relaxed font-serif">
        Formerly Professor of Psychology and Neuroscience at Skidmore College, Flip Phillips joined the faculty at the Rochester Institute of Technology’s MAGIC Center in 2019. His appointments span the School of Film and Animation and the Center for Imaging Science.
      </p>

      <h2>Career Trajectory & Interdisciplinary Roots</h2>
      <p>
        Phillips’ career trajectory began in the early 1980s in the school of architecture at <strong>The Ohio State University</strong>, attracted by its cross-disciplinary combination of art, design, engineering, and science. Introduced to the then-nascent world of computer graphics, he studied under computer graphics pioneer <strong>Charles Csuri</strong> at OSU's Computer Graphics Research Group (CGRG), earning his BFA in 1986.
      </p>
      <p>
        After his undergraduate training, Phillips taught and conducted research in medical imaging and 3D shape before joining the newly constituted <strong>Pixar</strong> — a spin-off from Lucasfilm and a hothouse of computational and visual experimentation. At Pixar, Phillips served as the original <em>‘Animation Scientist’</em> and technical director, creating tools for the Pixar Image Computer and even providing live reference movement for <em>Luxo Jr.</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        Returning to graduate study, serendipitous conversations with Pixar colleagues Alvy Ray Smith and Loren Carpenter, along with foundational texts by Jan Koenderink and Bela Julesz, pointed him toward visual science. He completed his Ph.D. in cognitive psychology at OSU in 1997, specializing in the perception of three-dimensional shape, haptics, and surface properties.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial, Memberships & Service</h2>
      <p>
        Phillips is a past editor of the <em>Mathematica Journal</em>, which focuses on computational mathematics across science, art, and modeling. He was inducted into the <strong>Visual Effects Society (VES)</strong> in 2025 and is an active member of the <strong>Vision Sciences Society (VSS)</strong>. He is also honored to be associated with <strong>Project Prakash</strong>, restoring sight to congenitally blind children and studying early sensory learning.
      </p>

      <h2>Machine Body & Extracurriculars</h2>
      <p>
        He is thankful to be part machine — <em>titanium, Dacron, and cow</em>. In his spare time, he can be found chopping out book reports and paradiddle-diddles on the snare with the Avant Garde Alumni Drumline, and documenting the history of drumming at <a href="https://drums.flipphillips.com" target="_blank">drums.flipphillips.com</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="my-8 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 not-prose">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 font-semibold mb-3">
          Contact & Coordinates
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200 font-mono">
          MAGIC Center &bull; Rochester Institute of Technology<br />
          300 Lomb Memorial Drive &bull; Rochester, NY 14623-5608<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:flip.phillips@rit.edu" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">flip.phillips@rit.edu</a>
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            href="/pubs/Flip%20Phillips%20External%20CV.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-xs font-mono font-semibold bg-neutral-900 text-white dark:bg-neutral-100 dark:text-neutral-900 hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
          >
            📄 Download CV (PDF)
          </a>
          <a
